  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 29db22c94e0641ef99312bf76573da3d, type: 3}
  m_Name: TutorialJournalDialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  speakerName: 
  sentences:
  - Like every passionate forager, you have your own forager's journal. Your forager's
    journal contains information about the forageables you may find in the wild.
    Press <sprite name="keys-Sheet_0"> to open your journal.
  - This page displays all the items you can find. Items that you have not yet discovered
    will not be labeled and will only be displayed as a silhouette. Try selecting
    one of the items to open the information page.
  - Here you will find details about the specific item. On the left page you can
    see its name, what it looks like, where it can be found and whether or not it
    is poisonous. On the right page you will find a short description of the item's
    physical aspects.
  - You can exit any menu by pressing <sprite name="keys-Sheet_21">.
  - Try looking around for items you can collect.
